<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Namibian Fishing half year slips into red.</title>
<headline>Namibian Fishing half year slips into red.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million Namibian dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     41.5 loss   vs 2.7 profit</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   13.63 loss  vs 0.86 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   14.00 loss  vs 2.07 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.07 charge vs 0.65 gain</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.86	  vs 0.71</p>
<p>    Turnover		  43.63	 vs 43.96</p>
<p>Full name: Namibian Fishing Industries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Namibia's Namfish said the hoped for improvement in the whitefish industry had not materialised. The firm said the sector was expected to recover slowly and it is reviewing its future in whitefish.</p>
<p>The firm also said that the pelagic fishing industry had also been through a difficult time, including the almost total absence of pilchards.</p>
<p>The firm said it did not anticipate an improvement in results for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
